<spell-notebook "tab theming">
	<header level="1">
		Tab
		<header>A tab is a hidden section of content activated by a menu.</>
	</>
	<tab-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			The tab menu adopts the [menu](/components/ui/ui-menu.html)'s stylesheet and the panes the segment's, so they read
			those families' `--ui-menu-*` and `--ui-segment-*` tokens: set them on the tab set or any ancestor.
			The set's own token, `--ui-tabs-pane-margin` (the space between the tab list and the panes), works
			the same way, or through `::part(tabs)`; attached and vertical sets swap it. Never set the `--_*`
			names: they're the sheets' private plumbing.

			Style the pieces with `::part()`: on `<ui-tabs>`, `tabs` (the whole set), `menu` (the tab list),
			`tab` (each tab button) and `icon`; on a `<ui-tab>`, `tab` is the pane's box.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-tabs {
			  --ui-tabs-pane-margin: 1.5em;
			}
			ui-tabs::part(tab) {
			  font-weight: 600;
			}
			ui-tab::part(tab) {
			  padding: 2em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-tab" playground>
				<ui-tabs appearance="tabular" attach="top" aria-label="Tabular demo">
					<ui-tab label="First">First</>
					<ui-tab label="Second">Second</>
					<ui-tab label="Third">Third</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			No theme restyles tabs themselves; the themes that restyle menus and segments reach the tab
			menu and the panes through those sheets. The one in the header applies a theme to the whole site.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
